    "narrative": "The primary engine of our offensive production today will be **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Nick Martinez and Barnett, respectively. **Lawrence Butler** is our standout play; he combines a strong base projection with a 19% boost from the opposing SP skill profile and an additional 13% from a dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** thrives in a prime #2 slot, with a 10% park boost and a massive 12% platoon edge, making him a high-efficiency anchor for the middle-infield and corner slots. **Zack Gelof** also projects well (66.86) as our lead-off and MI catalyst, capitalizing on the same soft matchup against Nick Martinez to provide consistent output.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing efficiency to manage our game caps. **Gleyber Torres** (53.11) was the final cut for the starting lineup; while his projection was respectable, a 13% negative platoon adjustment against Bibee lowered his expected ceiling compared to the higher-floor profiles of **Kyle Karros** and **Yainer Diaz**. We also avoided **JJ Bleday** and **Masyn Winn**, as both fell below our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold due to unfavorable matchups against elite SPs. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** closely, as the 31% rain risk introduces a volatility factor that could jeopardize his ability to complete his full complement of plate appearances. Meanwhile, keep an eye on **Yainer Diaz**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Kyle Karros**; their scores remain contingent on official lineup confirmation, though their current modeling\u2014boosted by wind conditions and favorable platoon splits\u2014suggests they are well-positioned to contribute if confirmed in their projected slots.",
